@startuml component-feature-layers
'' ============================================================================
'' vinary-viewer — Component: ADR-0028's composable rendering features (superseded by ADR-0029).
''
'' The layer model ADR-0028 recorded: recognition is the ONLY per-format layer; lowering, enrichment and
'' capability are shared feature modules that every dialect composes, both back-ends inherit, and raw HTML
'' crosses the one sanitize seam. ADR-0029 kept every shared layer and replaced the native recognizers with the
'' mature parsers — the note says so, because the figure documents a reversed design.
''
'' PlantUML over Mermaid: packages + concept tints from the shared _vv-theme palette, and a legend in the
'' house style (hue = concept: brown = source text, orange = IR core / features / ANSI, green = HTML,
'' amber = the one sanitize seam, grey = what ADR-0029 replaced).
'' ============================================================================
!include _vv-theme.iuml

'' the theme's dashed-grey «planned» look, named for what it marks here: a reversed design, not a forthcoming one
skinparam rectangle<<superseded>> {
  BackgroundColor PLANNED_COLOR
  BorderColor PLANNED_BORDER
  BorderStyle dashed
}

title Composable rendering features (ADR-0028) — recognition per format, everything downstream shared

left to right direction

package "Recognition — the only per-format layer" as REC {
  rectangle "**GFM**\nnative, deterministic\nblock + inline, O(n)\n(vinary.ir.recognizer.*)" <<superseded>> as GFM
  rectangle "**HTML**\ndelegated:\nrehype-parse + sanitizer" as HTML FS_TINT
  rectangle "**LaTeX**\ndelegated:\nunified-latex" as TEX FS_TINT
  rectangle "**Org**\ndelegated:\nuniorg (org-pipeline)" as ORG FS_TINT
  rectangle "**log**\nbrace-WPDA\nStreamParser" as LOG FS_TINT
}

rectangle "**common IR**\nvinary.ir.node\n(+ streaming spine,\nvinary.stream.*)" as IR IR_TINT

package "Shared feature layers — one module per construct, every dialect" as FEAT {
  rectangle "**Lowering**\n{:html :ansi} by IR :kind\n(both back-ends inherit)" as LOW IR_TINT
  rectangle "**Enrichment**\nordered post-lowering passes:\nmath · mermaid · figures · syntax" as ENR IR_TINT
  rectangle "**Capability**\nIR → derived views:\nTOC / outline · find index" as CAP IR_TINT
  rectangle "**registry/build**\nformat-spec + features → renderer\n(collision- and cycle-checked,\nmemoized once per format)" as REG IR_TINT
}

rectangle "**ir.backend.html**\n→ HTML → DOM (GUI)" as BH MARKDOWN_TINT
rectangle "**ir.backend.ansi**\n→ ANSI → terminal" as BA IR_TINT
rectangle "**lower-raw** — the ONE sanitize seam\nir→hast → rehype-raw →\nrehype-sanitize (GitHub allowlist) →\nstringify" as SAN IPC_TINT

GFM --> IR
HTML --> IR
TEX --> IR
ORG --> IR
LOG --> IR
IR --> REG
REG --> LOW
REG --> ENR
REG --> CAP
LOW --> BH
LOW --> BA
BH --> SAN : :raw-html leaves
ENR ..> BH
ENR ..> BA

note bottom of GFM
  **Superseded (ADR-0029).** The native recognizers were reversed
  before they shipped: the mature parsers (remark-gfm/micromark,
  uniorg, unified-latex) already deliver this, so the GFM box became
  a delegated recognizer too. Every shared layer to its right survived.
end note

legend right
  |= Colour |= Concept |
  |<#9F8766>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| a format's recognizer over its source text (delegated to a mature parser) |
  |<#DDDDDD>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| the native recognizer ADR-0029 replaced (dashed) |
  |<#E67E22>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| the IR core, the shared feature layers, the ANSI back-end |
  |<#67B11D>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| the HTML back-end (GUI) |
  |<#B1951D>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| the one sanitize seam for raw HTML |
endlegend
@enduml
